#only("1")[
#voiceover("One example of a decision-making framework is cost-benefit analysis. This involves systematically comparing the expected costs and benefits of different options to determine which one offers the best value.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("Another useful framework is a decision tree. This is a graphical tool that maps out the possible outcomes of a decision and helps identify the best course of action based on the probabilities and payoffs associated with each outcome.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Multi-criteria decision analysis is another framework that can help mitigate biases. This involves evaluating options based on a set of predefined criteria and assigning weights to each criterion based on its importance. This structured approach can help ensure that all relevant factors are considered and that the final decision is based on a balanced assessment of the available information.")
]
]

