#voiceover("Mitigating biases is crucial for improving financial decision-making. By reducing the influence of subjective factors and ensuring that choices are based on objective analysis, individuals and organizations can make more rational and informed decisions.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("Bias mitigation can also help avoid costly mistakes. Many financial errors are the result of biased thinking, such as overconfidence or loss aversion. By being aware of these biases and taking steps to overcome them, decision-makers can reduce the risk of making suboptimal choices that lead to negative outcomes.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Ultimately, mitigating biases can help achieve better financial outcomes. Whether it's making sound investment decisions, developing effective financial plans, or managing risk, reducing the impact of biases can lead to more successful and sustainable results over the long term.")
]
]

